{"id": "146857", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146857", "title": "Great Keppel Island", "text": "Great Keppel Island is an island off the coast of Yeppoon in the Australian state of Queensland.\nUnderstand.\nClimate.\nTropical Climate similar to the nearest city of Yeppoon. The average temperature in the summer reaches 24-30C while in the winter it drops to 12-22C.\nGet in.\nBy ferry.\nAll ferries leave from Keppel Bay Marina. There are 2 main ferry companies:\nBoth ferries make one voyage per day, 7 days a week.\nGet around.\nOn foot.\nThe island is fairly small with a bunch of trails around the island, from the resorts on the east to the lighthouse on the west is around 8km\nBy boat.\nGKI Watersports and Activities offers a dropoff service to any beach on the island for 90$ one way or 120$ return\nSleep.\nLodging.\nGreat Keppel Island Holiday Village is a resort on the island with 2 person cabins costing as much as 200$ per night\nGreat Keppel Island Hideaway is a resort on the island with 1-4 person houses costing as much as 230$ a night\nCamping.\nUnlike the surrounding Keppel Islands, there is no official camping spots on the island provided by the government.\nGreat Keppel Island Holiday Village has camp sites with minimum stay of 3 nights for 30$ a night"}
