{"id": "146878", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146878", "title": "Pinellas Park", "text": "Pinellas Park is in Florida. The city has some heavy industry and is home to a large variety of ethnic restaurants and businesses. The city is home to a variety of groups that have immigrated from all over the world.\nUnderstand.\nPinellas Park, incorporated in 1914, is in south-central Pinellas County. It is just northwest of St. Petersburg. As of 2015 it had a population of 49,079 persons.\nGet in.\nThe public bus system, Pinellas Suncoast Transit Authority (PSTA), operates buses that travel throughout Pinellas County. This is one way to enter Pinellas Park from another location in the county. The city can also be accessed by private vehicle or taxi.\nGet around.\nThe Pinellas Suncoast Transit Authority buses make various stops in Pinellas Park."}
{"id": "146880", "revid": "2361892", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146880", "title": "Calbiga", "text": "Calbiga is a growing agricultural and educational municipality of Samar Province in the Philippines. It lies along the Pan-Philippine (Maharlika) Highway and is said to be the land of beauty in the Province of Samar. \nUnderstand.\nThe town is famous for the Langun-Gobingob Caves which is the largest cave system in the Philippines, reputed to be the second largest in Asia and the world's third largest karst formation.\nGet in.\nThe nearest airport is in Tacloban ().\nDrink.\nTuba (coconut wine)"}
{"id": "146898", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146898", "title": "Alton (Hampshire)", "text": "\"Not to be confused with Alton, a village in Staffordshire near the Alton Towers theme park.\"\nAlton is a town in Hampshire, surrounded by attractive countryside and villages that were once home to novelist Jane Austen, naturalist Gilbert White, and Antarctic explorer Lawrence Oates.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nAlton is easiest accessed by car.\nDo.\nThe theme park Alton Towers is not anywhere near Alton in Hampshire. It is in the village of Alton in Staffordshire, about 185 miles north west."}
{"id": "146904", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146904", "title": "Mayport", "text": "Mayport is in northeastern Florida. The tiny town is right next to the Mayport Naval Station.\nDo.\nTake a ferry ride. See the lighthouse! Drive down the streets and you can see history. See The Church on Palmer and Ribault Park Drive in the Village."}
{"id": "146923", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146923", "title": "Nelakondapally", "text": "Nelakondapally is a town in East Telangana, India.\nUnderstand.\nThis is the birthplace of Kancherla Gopanna, popularly known as Ramadasu, who constructed Sri Rama temple in Bhadrachalam. It was hugely important during the times of Mahabharatha and Gauthama Buddha.\nGet in.\nBy road.\nThis spot is a major road junction on the routes from Khammam to Kodad and Kusumanchi."}
{"id": "146935", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146935", "title": "Stand-up comedy", "text": "Stand-up comedy is a minimalistic performing art, which originated in the United States and has spread around the world. It is performed on many levels, from free open-mic shows at dive bars, to stadium performances with world celebrities.\nDestinations.\nMost large English-speaking cities have a stand-up comedy scene, or at least comedians on tour. English-speaking comedy venues can be found even outside the Anglophone world, and are a good place to find English-speakers if you travel alone.\nBuy.\nSome high-end shows are available by pre-booking only. While some comedy clubs are free of charge, others are supported by tipping, or have a minimum drink policy for visitors.\nOther minimalist comedy styles.\nJapan is home to two minimalist styles of comedy, namely rakugo (\u843d\u8a9e), which involves a single performer seated on stage telling a story, with his only props being a fan and a handkerchief, and manzai (\u6f2b\u624d), which involves two performers misinterpreting each other and making puns.\nChina is home to a style of comedy known as xi\u00e0ngsh\u0113ng (\u76f8\u58f0) or crosstalk, which involves two performers having a dialogue in a strong Beijing accent, making use of exaggerated facial expressions and body language, wordplay and banter for comic effect.\nRespect.\nIn many cases, the master of ceremonies will open the performance with the house rules of conduct. Otherwise, they might be implicit, depending on venue.\nNormally, the only acceptable use of mobile phones is to take still pictures of the comedians, without flash. Audio or video recording of a comedy performance (including the crowd) is bad manners, as comedians are careful not to spread their material.\nConversely, the house might record the performance, including audience reactions, with or without request for consent.\nWhile a drink can make you more prone to laugh, don't get too drunk to enjoy the show.\nDon't heckle. You are likely to make the show worse for everyone. Have patience with rookies and less successful comedians; even the best comedians used to be in their shoes.\nComedy does commonly challenge taboos and norms, and the material might be offensive. If you cannot stand a performance, leave the room silently.\nAs in other hospitality venues, respect staff orders, whether they are from someone in the comedy crew, the waiter, or a bouncer."}
{"id": "146936", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=146936", "title": "Lobamba", "text": "Lobamba is the traditional capital of Eswatini, and home to around 11,000 citizens.\nUnderstand.\nWhereas Mbabane is the putative and political capital of the country, Lobamba is the traditional, spiritual, and legislative capital of this land, inside the Ezulwini Valley, or Valley of Heaven. It is touristy but still very aesthetic and peaceful.\nGet in.\nLobamba is about equidistant from Manzini or Mbabane, and King Mswati III International airport is about 75 km away. Try Transmagnific if you are in need of bus transportation within Eswatini, including to and from the airport.\nBuy.\nBesides looking at curios at the Manzenga Cultural Center, you can also shop at the Ezulwini Handicrafts Centre and the Gables Shopping Center.\nEat.\nThere are a lot of good choices around Lobamba. The Mantenga Cultural Village has traditional foods available as part of its cultural experience.\nSleep.\nNumerous places exist, including homestays and hostels like Legends Backpackers whose vibe kind of seems like something out of Vang Vieng.\nGo next.\nYou will probably either be going through Manzini or Mbabane."}
